From cfd63a1c113336bab2dd7ee9644454fee638abeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:39:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/17] drm/panfrost: Don't cancel a job that completed during
 a reset

A job that completes while panfrost_reset() has the schedulers stopped
gets its done fence signalled and its jc cleared, so panfrost_job_run()
returns NULL on resubmit and drm_sched_start() cancels it with
-ECANCELED. Return its done fence instead, so that it completes with its
own status. Depends on the previous patch. Not reproduced.

Fixes: 03877d621db0 ("drm/scheduler: mark jobs without fence as canceled")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Reported-by: Sashiko <sashiko-bot@kernel.org>
Closes: https://lore.kernel.org/all/sashiko-outbox-206581@kernel.org/
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_job.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_job.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_job.c
index 6dfbc33..4293eae 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_job.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_job.c
@@ -407,11 +407,14 @@ static struct dma_fence *panfrost_job_run(struct drm_sched_job *sched_job)
 	if (unlikely(job->base.s_fence->finished.error))
 		return NULL;
 
-	/* Nothing to execute: can happen if the job has finished while
-	 * we were resetting the GPU.
+	/* Nothing to execute: the job has finished (or failed) on the GPU
+	 * while we were resetting it, after drm_sched_stop() had detached the
+	 * scheduler from its done fence. Hand that fence back, so that the job
+	 * completes with the status the GPU gave it: with no fence,
+	 * drm_sched_start() would complete it as cancelled.
 	 */
 	if (!job->jc)
-		return NULL;
+		return dma_fence_get(job->done_fence);
 
 	fence = panfrost_fence_create(pfdev, slot);
 	if (IS_ERR(fence))
